Description: fix the audio format, the quit events and the timing
 * snd.c: the audio callback writes signed 16-bit mono samples at 44100 Hz,
   so SDL must convert them instead of being allowed to open the device
   with another format (SDL_AUDIO_ALLOW_ANY_CHANGE): with a device that
   prefers, for example, 32-bit float stereo, the samples were misread.
   Zero the SDL_AudioSpec and stop reading the sound buffer at its end.
 * seq.c: read all pending events each frame and also quit when the window
   is closed (SDL_QUIT); the close button did nothing before.
 * seq.c: give the effects the time elapsed since the start of the main
   loop, as the sound starts there, and not the time since SDL_Init, which
   includes the generation of the sound.
 * gfx.c: enable vsync after the creation of the OpenGL context, it had
   no effect before.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
